From: Richard T. Carback III <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: bus: Handle SDCA interrupts for class 0 devices with an IRQ domain

sdw_handle_slave_alerts() reads DP0_INT for the SDCA cascade only when the
peripheral reports a non-zero class ID. The Qualcomm WCD9378 in compute
mode reports class 0x00 in its DevId registers but raises SDCA interrupts
(GE Detected Mode on jack insertion), and its driver sets use_domain_irq.

The cascade was never seen, the nested SDCA IRQ never ran, SDCA_INT1 bit 4
was never acknowledged, and the bus looped on "Reached MAX_RETRY on alert
read" about 50 times per second from the first jack insertion on, with
jack detection never completing.

Also check the SDCA cascade when the driver asked for the SDCA IRQ domain.

Local test patch for the QN10 7.4-rc1 kernel build.
---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/bus.c b/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
index aeaae5a57..3af35f9be 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
@@ -1656,6 +1656,18 @@ static int sdw_handle_port_interrupt(struct sdw_slave *slave,
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * SDCA interrupts cascade through DP0. Devices normally say they are SDCA
+ * devices with a non-zero class ID, but some (the Qualcomm WCD9378 in
+ * compute mode) report class 0 and still use SDCA interrupts. Treat a
+ * driver that asked for the SDCA IRQ domain the same way; for any other
+ * device the cascade bit reads as zero.
+ */
+static bool sdw_slave_has_sdca_irq(struct sdw_slave *slave)
+{
+	return slave->id.class_id || slave->prop.use_domain_irq;
+}
+
 static int sdw_handle_slave_alerts(struct sdw_slave *slave)
 {
 	struct sdw_slave_intr_status slave_intr;
@@ -1693,7 +1705,7 @@ static int sdw_handle_slave_alerts(struct sdw_slave *slave)
 		goto io_err;
 	}
 
-	if (slave->id.class_id) {
+	if (sdw_slave_has_sdca_irq(slave)) {
 		ret = sdw_read_no_pm(slave, SDW_DP0_INT);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			dev_err(&slave->dev,
@@ -1833,7 +1845,7 @@ static int sdw_handle_slave_alerts(struct sdw_slave *slave)
 			goto io_err;
 		}
 
-		if (slave->id.class_id) {
+		if (sdw_slave_has_sdca_irq(slave)) {
 			ret = sdw_read_no_pm(slave, SDW_DP0_INT);
 			if (ret < 0) {
 				dev_err(&slave->dev,
